<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhawani Singh of Jhalawar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1874">1874</a>–<a href="/years/1929">1929</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bhawani Singh was Maharaj Rana of Jhalawar in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputana">Rajputana</a> from 1899 to 1929. Known for his learning and interest in education, he founded schools and a library and built the Bhawani Natyashala <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> in Jhalawar. His reign made the small state a noted centre of culture among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of Rajputana.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bhawani-singh-of-jhalawar.jpg" alt="Bhawani Singh of Jhalawar" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bassano Ltd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jhalawar-Maharaj-Rana-Sir-Shri-BHAWANI-SINGH-Bahadur-1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
